From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc: build mainline's ppc64le Rust support with GCC

7.3 enables Rust on powerpc upstream: HAVE_RUST for PPC32 and for
PPC64 && CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN, rustc's builtin powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu
target with -mma,-vsx,-hard-float,-altivec, BINDGEN_TARGET_powerpc and
ARCH_STATIC_BRANCH_ASM.  That replaces most of what this patch carried
for 7.2 (a generated target.json, the Kconfig select, the jump-label
macro).  With CC=gcc, 7.3.5 as released still does not build the Rust
side.  What is left here is what it needs:

- asm-compat.h: bindgen parses the kernel headers with libclang, which
  rejects GCC's "Y" constraint ("invalid input constraint 'YZ<>' in
  asm"), so no binding is generated at all.  Use the clang spelling
  under __BINDGEN__.

- rust/kernel/bug.rs: powerpc does not define ARCH_WARN_ASM, so the
  asm-based warn_flags! expands to the literal ARCH_WARN_ASM(...) and the
  kernel crate fails ("no rules expected `ARCH_WARN_ASM`") as soon as
  anything uses warn_on!, which 7.3's rust/kernel/sync/srcu.rs does.
  Route powerpc through the WARN_ON() helper, as loongarch and arm do.
  This one is not GCC-specific.

- arch/powerpc/Makefile: -Ccode-model=large for Rust modules, for the
  reason the comment above -mcmodel=large gives for C modules.

rustc 1.99 warns that disabling hard-float "is being phased out"; that
is upstream's flag set, kept as is.  Local patch for the Omarchy ppc64le
kernels.
---
--- a/arch/powerpc/Makefile
+++ b/arch/powerpc/Makefile
@@ -123,6 +123,9 @@
 	# kernel percpu data space (starting with 0xc...). We need a full
 	# 64bit relocation for this to work, hence -mcmodel=large.
 	KBUILD_CFLAGS_MODULE += -mcmodel=large
+	# Same for Rust modules: rustc's powerpc64le default is the medium
+	# model too.
+	KBUILD_RUSTFLAGS_MODULE += -Ccode-model=large
 endif
 endif
 
--- a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/asm-compat.h
+++ b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/asm-compat.h
@@ -37,7 +37,11 @@
 #define STDX_BE	stringify_in_c(stdbrx)
 #endif
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_CC_IS_CLANG
+/*
+ * bindgen parses these headers with libclang, which rejects GCC's "Y"
+ * constraint, so a GCC-built kernel takes the clang spelling there too.
+ */
+#if defined(CONFIG_CC_IS_CLANG) || defined(__BINDGEN__)
 #define DS_FORM_CONSTRAINT "Z<>"
 #else
 #define DS_FORM_CONSTRAINT "YZ<>"
